RG DS OS: both RG DS Plus panels at 59.9986 Hz instead of 60.17 Hz

The Plus's VOP clock is PLL 816 MHz / 13 = 62769231 Hz (the 62770 kHz the panels ask for). Front porches 127 and 14
instead of 120 and 16: 62769231 / (1311 x 798) = 59.9986 Hz. This is BananaLinux's banana-panel-tune search (the
smallest front porch change within 0.002 Hz of 60, each number keeping its digit count) run offline with that clock;
on a real Plus BananaLinux reports 60.17 -> 59.999 Hz from it. The sync and back porches are unchanged. Not yet seen
on our own Plus: if the panels stay dark, this patch is the first suspect.

--- a/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds-plus.dts
+++ b/rk3568-anbernic-rg-ds-plus.dts
@@ -514,7 +514,7 @@
 		panel_description =
 			"G size=87,66 delays=10,10,10,10,20 format=rgb888 lanes=2 flags=0xe03",
 
-			"M clock=62770 horizontal=1024,120,80,80 vertical=768,16,8,8 default=1",
+			"M clock=62770 horizontal=1024,127,80,80 vertical=768,14,8,8 default=1",
 
 			"I seq=3000",
 			"I seq=f749610200",
@@ -594,7 +594,7 @@
 		panel_description =
 			"G size=87,66 delays=10,10,10,10,20 format=rgb888 lanes=2 flags=0xe03",
 
-			"M clock=62770 horizontal=1024,120,80,80 vertical=768,16,8,8 default=1",
+			"M clock=62770 horizontal=1024,127,80,80 vertical=768,14,8,8 default=1",
 
 			"I seq=3000",
 			"I seq=f749610200",
